    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278">

                <pb facs="0340" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.51c39/311</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in El
                        Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 39</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-10-19">October 19, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: There is transmitted herewith for your
                    information a copy of a memorandum of a conversation held on October 16, 1934,
                    between Mr. F. J. Lisman, of the Bondholders Protective Committee for Republic
                    of El Salvador Bonds, and Assistant Secretary Welles,<anchor n="58"
                        xml:id="d278-f1"/> as well as a copy of a communication which Mr. Lisman
                    stated is being forwarded by air mail by the Bondholders Protective Committee to
                    the Minister of Finance of El Salvador.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d278-f2"/></p>
                <p>You will please inquire, orally and informally, of the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs what the views of his Government may be as regards the proposal of the
                    Bondholders Protective Committee that in the best interests of El Salvador and
                    of the bondholders an extension of the existing Agreement of May 5, 1933, be
                    effected to cover the calendar year 1935.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
